<p>Hail hits fast and unevenly, and your roof takes the impact whether you see it or not. A <strong>roof hail damage insurance claim in McAllen</strong> works best when it is handled carefully from the first day. Many disputed claims have nothing to do with whether damage exists. The trouble is that the damage was never properly identified, documented, or presented.</p>

<p>A common story goes like this. The roof looks fine from the driveway. A few weeks later a ceiling stain shows up. Months later the insurer says the damage is too old to be from the storm. This guide walks McAllen and Hidalgo County homeowners through the process, from the day of the storm to a settled claim, so you can avoid that outcome.</p>

<h2>Why roof hail claims matter in McAllen and the Rio Grande Valley</h2>

<p>Hail is a regular part of life in the Rio Grande Valley (RGV). The NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information (NCEI) Storm Events Database lists 163 hail reports for Hidalgo County from 1956 through 2025. Of those, 104 came in April or May, and 62 were golf-ball size (1.75 inches) or larger. Recent examples include:</p>

